vkquake-ios overlay 0029: menu touch — tap activates, DRAG scrolls.

Austin, device round on 1.1.0.1: "how can i scroll down the multiplayer list
via touch controls only? ... if i tap on the scroll bar on the left, it thinks
i tapped on that line item and tries to join that server."

Two defects, one gesture model.

1. There was no way to scroll a long list by touch at all. Fixed by splitting
   the single finger into TAP and DRAG at a slop threshold (6 menu units, ~12
   pt of glass at any interface scale): past the slop the gesture becomes a
   scroll, cancels the click it had armed, and emits K_MWHEELUP/K_MWHEELDOWN —
   one wheel step per row of finger travel, so the list tracks the thumb 1:1.
   Wheel keys are what makes this ~40 lines instead of a per-menu feature:
   M_HandleScrollBarKeys already handles both, and the server list, mods, key
   binds and game options all route their keys through it.

2. A tap that missed the rows still fired ENTER on whatever row the cursor had
   been left on — which on the server list joined a server the player never
   touched. M_Mouse_UpdateListCursor now records the rect it hit-tests, and a
   tap outside it does not activate. The rect is the menu's own, so the fix is
   menu-agnostic: it covers the gutter left of the server list and the gutter
   right of the mods list without either menu knowing about it. Taps ON the
   scrollbar are still passed through — M_HandleScrollBarKeys consumes them as
   a page jump, so they can never reach a row.

All menu touch state moves into menu.c behind M_TouchEvent, the one entry point
both real SDL finger events and the vkq_touch* console commands call. Those
commands exist because injected UIKit touches do not reach the touch path on a
simulator, so driving the real handler from the console is the only way to test
the gesture without a thumb on glass. vkq_slist_fake fills the host cache with a
deterministic scrollable list for the same reason.

